      "writtenOn": "2024-02-09T12:05:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t think we should worry about \"secure\" (non-non-secure) properties\n\nThe rationale for creating a separate node for host-controlled properties is not security but ABI.\n\nIn theory, reference tree (in uncompromised host as well) could have a node /avf/nonsecure* causing unnecessary conflicts (unless we explicitly mention in ABI, not to add that in refDT, which I would insist we don\u0027t).\n\n\n*changing name now, see reply at the other comment.",
      "parentUuid": "4d8842f7_b67bdacb",
