      "writtenOn": "2024-02-09T17:59:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e /avf/reference/avf-nonsecure? Or do we block that somewhere?\n\n@ptosi@google.com, I think we discussed the hack/solution to similar problem in ABL - it adds the relevant data only in `/avf/reference/avf` to avoid conflicting with other device nodes (like platform nodes perhaps?).\n\nAdding `/avf-untrusted/` is building up on the similar logic.\n\nLet us know what you think? Thanks",
      "parentUuid": "f029f915_c4efedd4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 45
      },
